{
	title: "Coolant Loop",
	x: 18.0d,
	y: 10.5d,
	text: [
		"Coolant is a closed loop. If you want to make power with nuclear, you can dump any (finite) amount of coolant into the system and it will be looped between the reactor and turbines forever. However, keep in mind that hot coolant turbines are fairly slow, so they may be the bottleneck for your setup."
